📚 Student Study Planner Dashboard
Day 18 — 60-Day Claude AI Challenge
A single-file, interactive study planner dashboard built for students juggling coursework, internships, and side projects. No build step, no dependencies — just open the HTML file and go.
✨ Features
Task Manager — add, complete, and delete tasks with priority levels (High / Medium / Low) and due dates
Live Stats — tasks completed today, upcoming deadlines, focus sessions, and high-priority items at a glance
Focus Timer — built-in Pomodoro-style timer (25 min focus / 5 min break) with an animated progress ring
Subject Progress Tracker — visual progress bars for each subject/course
Weekly Timetable — color-coded schedule view (lectures, internships, free time) with mobile-friendly horizontal scroll
🎨 Design
Dark theme with a violet accent palette
Typography: Space Grotesk (headings) + JetBrains Mono (data, labels, timestamps)
Fully responsive — works on mobile, tablet, and desktop
Zero external JS frameworks — pure HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript
🛠️ Tech Stack
HTML5 / CSS3 (custom properties, grid, flexbox)
Vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks, no build tools)
Google Fonts (Space Grotesk, JetBrains Mono)
🚀 Usage
Clone or download this repo
Open student_study_planner.html in any browser
Start adding tasks and tracking your study sessions — all data is in-memory for this version (resets on refresh)
